From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:32:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: panorama comfortable grid sizes cells to wide covers

The library's "Panorama comfortable grid" kept the 2:3 book-shaped cell
and only switched the image to ContentScale.Fit, so a 16:9 thumbnail
(every XVideos cover, for instance) was letterboxed with large empty
bands above and below and ended up smaller than in the plain grid. The
browse grid already passes fitToPanoramaCover = true, which turns the
cell itself into the 3:2 panorama shape; do the same in the library.
Portrait covers (ratio > 0.75) are unaffected.

Harmony-only: Mihon has no panorama cover feature, Animeko has no such grid.
---
 .../presentation/library/components/LibraryComfortableGrid.kt  | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/presentation/library/components/LibraryComfortableGrid.kt b/app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/presentation/library/components/LibraryComfortableGrid.kt
index 828685a..0ddf28f 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/presentation/library/components/LibraryComfortableGrid.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/presentation/library/components/LibraryComfortableGrid.kt
@@ -71,6 +71,9 @@ internal fun LibraryComfortableGrid(
                 },
                 // KMK -->
                 usePanoramaCover = usePanoramaCover,
+                // Harmony: size the cell to the wide cover like the browse grid does, instead of
+                // letterboxing a 16:9 thumbnail inside a 2:3 book-shaped cell.
+                fitToPanoramaCover = true,
                 // KMK <--
             )
         }
